   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A single variable is a special case.</p>\n<p>Make a table of values.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><b><i>x</i></b></td>\n<td><b><i>y</i></b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>–3</td>\n<td>–4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>–4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>–4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Plot the points and connect them with a line.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBZ2NOIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--ee4dd51ecfad379effd979e278a49b6f6489e2f6/CS_Figure_05_08_024.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 1. The line is horizontal and it passes through the following points, (negative 2, negative 4), (0, negative 4), and (2, negative 4). Note: all values are approximate.\">"
    }
   ],
